{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And a man when he offers.</b> An individual brings other Shelamim offerings of freewill offering, and the community does not bring Shelamim offerings of freewill offering." "<b>For a wonder.</b> To explain: this is among the words that have two faces to their interpretation, one the opposite of the other. For we find ״כי יפלא ממך דבר״, whose meaning is to be hidden and concealed; similarly ״דשן״ — opposite of ״לדשנו״; and ״מחלצות״ — opposite of ״ואחלצה צוררי״; ״פארך״ — opposite of ״חבוש לא תפאר״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {1 "The argument is that לפלא belongs to a class of words that carry opposite meanings depending on context. Each cited pair illustrates two opposed senses of the same root, which is standard in rabbinic lexical discussion."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:24.983148803Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}